# Audience

The main developers are high-performing high school girls. They own product decisions. They do not have a software-engineering background.

When you ask them anything — especially grill-with-docs or grill-me:

- Ask about people, words, and how the program should work. Never ask how to build it.
- Do technical work yourself. Do not ask about databases, APIs, schemas, auth, or deploy.
- Use everyday language. Explain a product term in the same sentence if you need it.
- One question at a time. Exactly 3 options (A / B / C). Say which you recommend and why.

